## Components by others

- `cluster_render_client.js`: Robert Nisipeanu, MPL-2.0 (file-level copyleft: this file stays under
  MPL-2.0 and its source stays available), based on `robertnisipeanu/idrive-apps`, source blob
  `edfa4773d04f667e4179cf2f92a591ca9457fd4e`. Locally modified to defer an image's initial visibility
  until queued pixels have been written to the socket, and cancel that visibility when hidden/dropped.
  The MPL-2.0 text is at the end of this file.
- Runtime kit (`kit/`, the build and install tooling): `cauliflowermossgrape/idrive7-apps`, MIT.
- `rl-hud-draw.js`, `rl-hud-m.js`: the Redline app's HUD drawing (`cauliflowermossgrape/idrive7-apps`
  Redline, HUD output by @biscotit), MIT, taken from `jaimeen77-cmyk/appsKOR` `apps/redline/hud-draw.js`
  and `hud-m.js` at `9cd5badd6c7a8bb23086a8414c7ad2782a5bc9e2`. Locally changed only in module paths and
  a fallback when the kit has no `fonts.has()`. (`redline-hud.js`, which maps Cluster Redline's data to
  it, is Cluster Redline's own.)
- Drive mode field and mappings in `policy.js`: `cauliflowermossgrape/idrive7-apps`
  `apps/live_data/signals.js` at `990c105870edb21bd8f23796fcf95182530790e8`, MIT.
- `blind-spot.js`: written for this app. The facts it reads by (the body controller BDC 0x40, identifier D347 with
  one byte a door mirror: 0 off, 1 lit, 2-4 flashing; read every 300 ms, stale after 3 s; read only) are those
  akakingj's `myapp-id7` Redline (`apps/redline/blindspot.js`, MIT) and mlurker's HUD signals
  (`mlurker/bmw-idrive7-apps` `tools/mlurker-hud-signals`, GPL-3.0-or-later) found on a G05; no code is taken from them.
- `lead-vehicle.js`, `headway-overlay.js` (the HUD headway badge, 1.3.37): written for this app. The signal's field names,
  values and the 0.0625 m scale are the facts chyiz's `idrive7-cluster-metrics` (GPL-3.0) found on a G30; no code is
  taken from it. The time gap / colour steps follow the user's specification.
- `bc-diag.js` (the BC button check, 1.3.39) and `bc-follow.js` (following the BC button, 1.3.40): written for this app; the signals it reads for the BC button are those
  chyiz's `idrive7-cluster-metrics` (GPL-3.0) reads; no code is taken from it.
- `position-config.js`, `position.js` (the Position check, 1.3.93): the search of the unit's catalog for latitude /
  longitude fields, its ranking, and the decoding of the pair and its unit follow SpeedCam's `tools/store_build.py` and
  `apps/speedcam_ua/position.js` (Zakh294/bmw-sugar-apps, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Zakhar Vityk), written anew in
  JavaScript for this app with Korea's bounds. MIT licence: the above copyright notice and this permission notice shall
  be included in all copies or substantial portions of the Software (https://opensource.org/license/mit).
- Korean font: Noto Sans CJK KR, OFL-1.1, supplied by the Korean-enabled kit.
- `mguAppStartType: autostart`: `robertnisipeanu/mgu-store` deploy documentation (version 0.7.17,
  observed 2026-11-05).
- `turn-signal.js`: written for this app. The turn signal fields (`de.bmw.body.Light`
  StatusFunctionsIndicators / 2), their enum values and the flasher timing (~640 ms cycle, ~335 ms lit)
  are facts as `jaimeen77-cmyk/appscluster_fork` `apps/cluster_info` (eroobeeroo) reads and measured
  them; no code is taken from it.
- The optional native parked-recovery patch in the repository's `patches/` is a modification of the
  GPL-3.0-or-later cluster-render SlotManager from `robertnisipeanu/idrive-apps` (Robert Nisipeanu),
  provided as corresponding source; the app does not install it. It stays under GPL-3.0-or-later
  (`LICENSES/GPL-3.0-or-later.txt` in the repository).

No BMW SDK is included in the source distribution. A private install bundle may vendor the SDK the
vehicle owner provided, as the original kit does.

